# Git push / pull (MagicSquare_XX)

When running `git push` or `git pull` for this repository:

1. **Do not** put tokens in chat, commits, or `git config`.
2. Load credentials from project root `.env` (gitignored): `GITHUB_USER`, `GITHUB_TOKEN`, `GITHUB_REPO`.
3. Use an authenticated remote URL for the operation only:

```powershell
# From repo root — load .env into process env
Get-Content .env | ForEach-Object {
  if ($_ -match '^\s*([^#][^=]+)=(.*)$') {
    Set-Item -Path "env:$($matches[1].Trim())" -Value $matches[2].Trim()
  }
}
$authUrl = "https://${env:GITHUB_USER}:${env:GITHUB_TOKEN}@github.com/${env:GITHUB_USER}/${env:GITHUB_REPO}.git"

# Examples (replace branch as needed)
git push $authUrl HEAD:develop
git pull $authUrl develop
```

4. Keep `origin` as the plain HTTPS URL (`https://github.com/jbjbljb/MagicSquare_XX.git`) — do not embed tokens in `.git/config`.
5. If `.env` is missing, ask the user to copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in values; do not ask them to paste tokens in chat.
